'''Phase Five''' is the fifth phase of the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]], and the second phase of [[The Multiverse Saga]].

==Overview==
Phase Five served as a pivotal middle chapter in the Multiverse Saga, exploring deep dives into new characters ([[Echo]], [[Agatha Harkness|Agatha]]), continuing legacy heroes ([[Ant-Man]], [[Guardians of the Galaxy|Guardians]]), introducing new threats like [[Kang the Conqueror|Kang]] and [[Cassandra Nova]], and establishing the darker, more grounded, and chaotic tone of the multiverse, setting up future team-ups and multiversal conflicts. Key themes included the consequences of multiversal events such as [[Deadpool & Wolverine]] introducing Anchor beings, legacy of the [[Captain America]] mantle with [[Captain America|Sam Wilson]] in [[Captain America: Brave New World]], anti-heroes such as [[Thunderbolts*]] (a.k.a. '''The New Avengers'''), and a blend of cosmic and street-level stories ranging from [[The Marvels]] or [[Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania]] to [[Secret Invasion (TV series)|Secret Invasion]] or [[Daredevil: Born Again]].

==Projects==
===''[[Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania]]'' (2023)===
[[Scott Lang]] and [[Hope van Dyne]], along with Hope's parents, [[Hank Pym]] and [[Janet van Dyne]], and Lang's daughter, [[Cassie Lang|Cassie]], go on a new adventure exploring the [[Quantum Realm]] that pushed their limits and pits them against [[Kang the Conqueror]].<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/ant-man-and-the-wasp-quantumania-special-look-ccxp22 Special Look at 'Ant-Man and The Wasp: Quantumania' Debuts at CCXP22]</ref>

===''[[Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3]]'' (2023)===
In [[Marvel Studios]]' ''Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3'' our beloved [[Guardians of the Galaxy|band of misfits]] are settling into life on [[Knowhere]]. But it isn't long before their lives are upended by the echoes of [[Rocket]]'s turbulent past. [[Peter Quill]], still reeling from the loss of [[Gamora]], must rally his team around him on a dangerous mission to save Rocket's life—a mission that, if not completed successfully, could quite possibly lead to the end of the Guardians as we know them.<ref>[https://thedirect.com/article/guardians-of-the-galaxy-vol-3-rocket-fate Disney Teases Rocket’s Dire Fate In Guardians Vol. 3]</ref>

===''[[Secret Invasion (TV series)|Secret Invasion]]'' (2023)===
====[[Secret Invasion  (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2023)====
In ''Secret Invasion'', set in the [[2026|present-day]] [[Marvel Cinematic Universe|MCU]], [[Nick Fury|Fury]] learns of a clandestine [[Secret Invasion|invasion]] of [[Earth]] by a [[Skrull Resistance|faction]] of shapeshifting [[Skrulls]]. Fury joins his allies, including [[Everett Ross]], [[Maria Hill]], and the Skrull [[Talos]], who has made a life for himself on Earth. Together they race against time to thwart an imminent Skrull invasion and save [[Humans|humanity]].<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/secret-invasion-trailer-poster Trust No One in the New Trailer for 'Secret Invasion']</ref>

===''[[I Am Groot]]'' (2022-2023)===
====[[I Am Groot/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
The troublemaking twig returns to mischief in the second season of ''I Am Groot''. This time, Baby [[Groot]] finds himself exploring the universe and beyond aboard the [[Guardians of the Galaxy|Guardians]]' spaceships, coming face-to-face—or nose-to-nose—with new and colorful creatures and environments.<ref>[https://whatsondisneyplus.com/marvels-i-am-groot-season-2-trailer-released-disney-release-date-announced/ Marvel’s “I Am Groot” Season 2 Trailer Released & Disney+ Release Date Announced]</ref>

===''[[Loki (TV series)|Loki]]'' (2021-2023)===
====[[Loki (TV series)/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
''Loki'' Season 2 picks up in the aftermath of the shocking season finale when [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] finds himself in a battle for the soul of the [[Time Variance Authority]]. Along with [[Mobius M. Mobius]], [[Hunter B-15]] and a team of new and returning characters, Loki navigates an ever-expanding and increasingly dangerous [[multiverse]] in search of [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Sylvie]], Judge [[Ravonna Renslayer|Renslayer]], [[Miss Minutes]] and the truth of what it means to possess free will and glorious purpose.<ref>[https://coveredgeekly.com/new-loki-season-2-cast-members-extended-synopsis-revealed/ New ‘Loki’ Season 2 Cast Members, Extended Synopsis Revealed]</ref>

===''[[The Marvels]]'' (2023)===
In ''The Marvels'', [[Carol Danvers]] aka Captain Marvel has reclaimed her identity from the tyrannical [[Kree]] and [[Battle at Mar-Vell's Laboratory|taken revenge]] on the [[Supreme Intelligence]]. But unintended consequences see Carol shouldering the burden of a destabilized universe. When her duties send her to an anomalous [[wormhole]] linked to a [[Dar-Benn|Kree revolutionary]], her powers become entangled with that of [[Jersey City]] super-fan [[Kamala Khan]], aka Ms. Marvel, and Carol's estranged niece, now [[S.A.B.E.R.]] astronaut Captain [[Monica Rambeau]]. Together, this unlikely trio must team up and learn to work in concert to save the universe as "The [[Marvels]]".<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/marvels-teaser-trailer-carol-danvers-monica-rambeau-kamala-khan 'The Marvels': New Teaser Trailer Sends Carol Danvers, Monica Rambeau, and Kamala Khan on a Cosmic Adventure]</ref>

===''[[What If...?]]'' (2021-2024)===
====[[What If...?/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
[[What If...?/Season Two|Season 2]] of ''What If...?'' continues the journey as [[The Watcher]] guides viewers through the vast [[Multiverse]], introducing brand new and familiar faces throughout the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]]. The series questions, revisits and twists classic Marvel Cinematic moments with an incredible voice cast that includes a host of stars who reprise their iconic roles.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/what-if-season-2-trailer ‘What If…?’: Unwrap New Season 2 Trailer Now]</ref>

===''[[Echo (TV series)|Echo]]'' (2024)===
====[[Echo (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
''Echo'' spotlights [[Maya Lopez]] as she is pursued by [[Wilson Fisk]]'s criminal empire. When the journey brings her home, she must confront her own family and legacy.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/echo-director-sydney-freeland-maya-lopez-kingpin ‘Echo’ Director Sydney Freeland Teases What’s Ahead for Maya Lopez]</ref>

===''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024)===
[[Marvel Studios]] presents their most significant mistake to date—"Deadpool & Wolverine." A listless [[Wade Wilson]] toils away in civilian life. His days as the morally flexible mercenary, Deadpool, behind him. When his [[Earth-10005|homeworld]] faces an existential threat, Wade must reluctantly [[Deadpool Suit|suit-up]] again with an even more reluctantlier… reluctanter? Reluctantest? He must convince a reluctant [[Wolverine]] to— ''Fuck''. Synopses are so fucking stupid.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/deadpoolwolverine/#!asset/b5tx8p3cshmx9s9r5g4pkz83 DEADPOOL WOLVERINE Synopsis REV 5-16-24.pdf]</ref>

===''[[Agatha All Along]]'' (2024)===
====[[Agatha All Along/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
The infamous [[Agatha Harkness]] finds herself down and out of power after a suspicious goth [[teen]] helps [[Liberation of Agatha Harkness|break her free]] from a distorted spell. Her interest is piqued when he begs her to take him on the legendary [[Witches' Road]], a magical gauntlet of trials that, if survived, rewards a witch with what they’re missing. Together, Agatha and this mysterious teen [[Search for Coven Members|pull together]] a desperate [[Agatha Harkness' Coven|coven]], and [[Walking of the Witches' Road|set off]] down, down, down The Road…<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/agatha-all-along-first-trailer Kathryn Hahn’s Agatha Harkness Returns in 'Agatha All Along' Trailer]</ref>

===''[[What If...?]]'' (2021-2024)===
====[[What If...?/Season Three|Season Three]] (2024)====
[[Marvel Animation|Marvel's animated]] series ''What If...?'' returns in [[What If...?/Season Three|Season 3]] for its culminating adventure through the [[multiverse]]. Watch as classic characters make unexpected choices that will mutate their worlds into spectacular alternate versions of the [[MCU]]. [[The Watcher]] will guide viewers as the series traverses new genres, bigger spectacles, and incredible new characters.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/whatifseason3/#!asset/n3ww5p6q6xrxx5ztwh689x WHAT IF Season 3 Project Profile 10.30.24.pdf]</ref> 

===''[[Captain America: Brave New World]]'' (2025)===
[[Anthony Mackie]] returns as the high-flying hero [[Sam Wilson]], who's officially taken up the mantle of Captain America. After meeting with newly elected [[United States|U.S.]] President [[Thaddeus Ross]], Sam finds himself in the middle of an [[Battle of Celestial Island|international incident]]. He must discover the reason behind a nefarious [[Earth|global]] [[Ruination of Thaddeus Ross' Legacy|plot]] before the true [[Leader|mastermind]] has the entire world seeing red.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/movies/captain-america-brave-new-world ''Captain America: Brave New World'' on Marvel.com]</ref>

===''[[Daredevil: Born Again]]'' (2025-TBA)===
====[[Daredevil: Born Again/Season One|Season One]] (2025)====
[[Matt Murdock]], a blind lawyer with heightened abilities, fights for justice through his bustling [[Murdock & McDuffie|law firm]], while former mob boss [[Wilson Fisk]] pursues his own political endeavors in [[New York City|New York]]. When their past identities begin to emerge, both men find themselves on an inevitable collision course.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/daredevilbornagain/#!asset/nw58khrjw347nvbqbqthppz ''Daredevil: Born Again'' Project Profile]</ref>

===''[[Thunderbolts*]]'' (2025)===
[[Marvel Studios]] assembles an unconventional [[New Avengers|team]] of antiheroes—[[Yelena Belova]], [[Bucky Barnes]], [[Red Guardian]], [[Ghost]], [[Taskmaster]] and [[John Walker]]. After finding themselves [[Battle at the O.X.E. Vault|ensnared]] in a [[O.X.E. Vault|death trap]] set by [[Valentina Allegra de Fontaine]], these disillusioned castoffs must embark on a dangerous [[Attack on Manhattan|mission]] that will force them to confront the darkest corners of their pasts. Will this dysfunctional group tear themselves apart, or find redemption and unite as something much more before it’s too late?<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/movies/thunderbolts ''Thunderbolts*'' on Marvel.com]</ref>

===''[[Ironheart (TV series)|Ironheart]]'' (2025)===
====[[Ironheart (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2025)====
Set after the events of ''[[Black Panther: Wakanda Forever]]'', [[Marvel Television]]'s ''Ironheart'' pits technology against magic when [[Riri Williams]]—a young, genius inventor determined to make her mark on the world—returns to her hometown of [[Chicago]]. Her unique take on building [[:Category:Ironheart Armors|iron suits]] is brilliant, but in pursuit of her ambitions, she finds herself wrapped up with the mysterious yet charming [[Parker Robbins]] aka “The Hood”.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/tv-shows/ironheart/1 ''Ironheart'' on Marvel.com]</ref>

